# Response headers for Cloudflare Workers Static Assets.
# Mirrors the header rules that vercel.json defines, so the site behaves the
# same on either host. Copied verbatim into dist/ by Vite.
#
# Note on Strict-Transport-Security: it tells browsers to use HTTPS for a year
# after the first visit, so it only protects repeat visitors. The very first
# plain-HTTP request still needs Cloudflare's "Always Use HTTPS" redirect, which
# is a dashboard setting. The "preload" directive is omitted on purpose, since
# enrolment in the browser preload list is slow and awkward to undo.
#
# Comments must stay at column 0. Inside an indented rule block a line is parsed
# as a header, not as a comment.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains

# Hashed filenames, so the content behind a URL never changes.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
